WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.830
Mike, give us the next story.

2
00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:02.663
Okay.

3
00:00:02.663 --> 00:00:07.270
So CNN reports, one homeowner in South Lake, Tahoe,

4
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.160
got a fun springtime surprise.

5
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.810
They'd been hearing a purring sound

6
00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.850
under the floorboards for months.

7
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:17.850
Turns out there were bears under their house.

8
00:00:17.948 --> 00:00:18.781
Whoa.

9
00:00:18.781 --> 00:00:19.660
A full family of bears.

10
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.610 line:15%
A mama bear and four baby cubs.

11
00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.210 line:15%
Oh, my gosh.
It's so adorable.

12
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.310 line:15%
Experts say the homeowner was probably hearing

13
00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.250 line:15%
the bear's cozy hibernation sounds.

14
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.990 line:15%
Snoring, breathing, nursing, maybe some rolling around.

15
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.510 line:15%
The bears have safely returned to the forest.

16
00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:35.343 line:15%
Good ending.

17
00:00:35.343 --> 00:00:36.920 line:15%
My sister, Patty and I,

18
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.610 line:15%
years ago, we went to Alaska.

19
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.760
We went to this place called Katmai National Park.

20
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.070
You go to bear orientation when you show up

21
00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:45.157
and they teach you, if you ever see a bear

22
00:00:45.157 --> 00:00:45.990
What to do?

23
00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:46.823
You're supposed to clap, yeah.

24
00:00:46.823 --> 00:00:47.656
Clap?

25
00:00:47.656 --> 00:00:49.010
You go, (claps) "I'm right here, bear.

26
00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:49.843
I'm right here. (claps)

27
00:00:49.843 --> 00:00:50.780
I'm Mike. (claps)

28
00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:51.730
You're a bear (claps)."

29
00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.709
You know, just make noise, right?

30
00:00:53.709 --> 00:00:54.542
Really?

31
00:00:54.542 --> 00:00:55.480
So I was fly fishing

32
00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.760 line:15%
with this guide and my sister Patty,

33
00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.980 line:15%
and I hear my sister, Patty go, "Mike!"

34
00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.020 line:15%
and I look around, there's a bear,

35
00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.510 line:15%
about probably 25 feet from-

36
00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:05.343 line:15%
That's close.
Yeah, I know.

37
00:01:05.343 --> 00:01:06.176 line:15%
It was wild.

38
00:01:06.176 --> 00:01:08.620
And I was so scared, I froze up.

39
00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:11.290
And then the guide,

40
00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:12.730
I'll step up for a second to explain this,

41
00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.780
but it's like the guide snapped into action,

42
00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.153
he sprinted at the bear and he goes,

43
00:01:17.153 --> 00:01:18.201
"He-yah! (claps)

44
00:01:18.201 --> 00:01:19.113
He-yah! (claps)

45
00:01:19.113 --> 00:01:20.790
He-yah! (claps)
(Drew laughs)

46
00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.700
And the bear just walked away,

47
00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:24.320
like "I'm a bear", et cetera.

48
00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.260
And I was so relieved

49
00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.840
that my sister didn't get eaten by the bear.

50
00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:31.097
But then I was a little mad 'cause I was like,

51
00:01:31.097 --> 00:01:33.290
"You know, you didn't tell me about the He-yah! plan."

52
00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:34.150
Yeah.
Yeah.

53
00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:36.599
You told me to go (claps limply) "I'm right here, bear."

54
00:01:36.599 --> 00:01:37.960
Yeah.
"I'm right here."

55
00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.340
Okay, and finally.
(sighs) Oh my gosh.

56
00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.780
We have a big wedding kerfuffle out of the UK.

57
00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.970
Ooh, Mike, I think this one's gonna speak to you.

58
00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.490
This comes from The Mirror.

59
00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:48.750
The groomsman got into hot water with the bride

60
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.397
because he secretly ordered pizza to the parking lot.

61
00:01:51.397 --> 00:01:52.288
(Mike laughs)

62
00:01:52.288 --> 00:01:53.900
He says the veggies and salad at the reception

63
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:55.130 line:15%
were not cutting it.

64
00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:57.030 line:15%
He needed a little more "fuel",

65
00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:59.470 line:15%
so he ordered pizza to his car, covertly.

66
00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.010 line:15%
But unfortunately, the other guests joins in.

67
00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:04.690 line:15%
And when the bride caught the groom, himself,

68
00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:07.303 line:15%
biting into a cheesy slice, she lost it.

69
00:02:08.585 --> 00:02:11.376 line:15%
(Drew mimics hysterical screaming)

70
00:02:11.376 --> 00:02:14.210 line:15%
This is, you know, bridal dresses flying.

71
00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.740 line:15%
Pizza's a solution for most things.

72
00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.460
Totally.
(audience applauds)

73
00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:21.020
Totally.
Especially on Drew's News

74
00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:22.083
A pizza pillow.

75
00:02:23.441 --> 00:02:25.520
I know we do have plates out here, it's weird.

76
00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:26.353
I don't know why.

77
00:02:26.353 --> 00:02:28.556
Why do we have plates out here?

78
00:02:28.556 --> 00:02:30.150
Oh my God, Kat!

79
00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.485
Oh my God. (laughs)

80
00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.653
(audience applauds)

81
00:02:34.653 --> 00:02:36.423
Oh my gosh.
Are you kidding?

82
00:02:36.423 --> 00:02:40.402
Thank you, Kat, so much. (screams excitedly)

83
00:02:40.402 --> 00:02:41.704
Get in, get in.

84
00:02:41.704 --> 00:02:43.710
(audience cheers and applauds)

85
00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:44.543
Birbigs.

86
00:02:44.543 --> 00:02:46.279
This is too much.

87
00:02:46.279 --> 00:02:47.112
Get in.

88
00:02:47.112 --> 00:02:47.945
I'm doing the right thing

89
00:02:47.945 --> 00:02:49.300
by serving you guys first, that's love.

90
00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.330
When I show up on a talk show and you serve me pizza,

91
00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:55.285
I know I have a problem.

92
00:02:55.285 --> 00:02:57.220
(Ross laughs)
(audience applauds)

93
00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.053
Or-

94
00:02:58.053 --> 00:02:59.230
No, you gotta figure it out.

95
00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:01.600
We're just that awesome show

96
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:04.847
that wants to, like pizza, deliver.

97
00:03:04.847 --> 00:03:06.060
Oh, Drew!

98
00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.060
Rossy, are you proud?

99
00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:08.700
I'm very proud of you.

100
00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:12.117
Well, Mike Birbiglia, get more Mike on his podcast,

101
00:03:12.117 --> 00:03:13.870
"Mike Birbiglia's Working It Out",

102
00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:16.460
and I'm saying all of this with pizza in my mouth,

103
00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.230
to honor your love of pizza.

104
00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:21.340
And he has a solo show, "The Old Man and the Pool",

105
00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.830
and it is coming to Chicago and LA,

106
00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:25.350
so check the website for tickets.

107
00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:26.401 line:15%
I will be there.

108
00:03:26.401 --> 00:03:29.484 line:15%
(bright theme music)

